extraction_notes: "Page span: the heading, race, attributes, bonuses and O.C.C. skills fill the right column of printed 188; the related skills, equipment, money and cybernetics fill printed 189 under a full-column illustration. Lt. Jack Crazy Cavanaugh''s stat block follows on printed 190 and is an NPC, not part of this class. The book heads it NTSET Protector O.C.C.; the survey''s Protector / Hunter name is not printed on the heading. RACE: Human or Psi-Stalker; see race_restrictions. GROUP: men-of-arms. The NTSET section prints no Rifts O.C.C. grouping; this is the division''s human combat operative, an elite strike-team police officer with unchangeable Martial Arts and heavy weapons, so men_of_arms true. BONUSES: initiative +1 at levels 1, 4 and 9; +1 vs magic illusion and mind control, and +1 vs magic of all kinds (stored on spell_magic and ritual_magic); +1 vs possession at 1, 4, 9 and 12; +2 vs horror factor at 2, 4, 7, 10, 12 and 15. HAND TO HAND: Martial Arts, printed as unchangeable, so the price block is empty. MOS: four +10% skills from one of seven areas (Espionage, Mechanical, Medical, Physical, Piloting, Science, Rogue), modelled as skills.mos; Piloting is the Pilot category. RELATED SKILLS: printed as two skills at levels one, four, eight and twelve; stored literally as two at each level. MONEY: 3D6x1000 credits to start as printed, confirmed from a render because the text layer ciphers it; the salary is prose. ARMOR: the book''s old style Dead Boy armor is CA-1 heavy or CA-2 light (printed 104). E-clips: four for each weapon, stored as eight. The flares are stored as signal flares, the flash grenades as stun/flash grenades, the tear gas grenades as the Tear Gas Grenade row, the nightstick as the fiberglass row, the silver plated survival knife as the silver plated knife and the silver cross as the small silver cross. Vehicles are prose, as the Side Kick RPA does; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3."
